(property "Description" " | design | W2 CTRL-6 (recipe of build/15 \"Захист VSYS Pico за D301\", reviews RV4-E-3/RV4-S-1): PTC ahead of the Pico VSYS limiter U316, so that the IN/EN copper of U316 and an IN-GND bridge of its SOT-23-6 (pin 1 IN next to pin 2 GND) are limited by the PTC and never by F102 4 A alone; on CTRL its LAB5 pad 1 sits on the 1.85 mm LAB5 feed, so no LAB5 copper narrower than the class width reaches a SOT-23-6 pin. Bourns MF-MSMF050: Vmax 15 V, Imax 100 A, Ihold 0.50 A / Itrip 1.00 A at 23 C, Ihold 0.77 A at -40 C, 0.68 A at -20 C, 0.33 A at 70 C, Rmin 0.15 ohm, R1max 1.0 ohm, 8.0 A trips in 0.15 s max, tripped dissipation 0.8 W typ (REV. BE 09/26, read 2026-11-22). The smallest family member whose 70 C Ihold (0.33 A) holds the U316 maximum limit IOSmax 0.223 A (R397 140k): a VSYS short is handled by U316 alone, the PTC trips only on a fault ahead of U316. Its series resistance (Rmin 0.15 ohm to R1max 1.0 ohm) is in the Pico VSYS path: with U316 rDS(on) (135 mOhm max) it lowers VSYS by 0.04-0.17 V at 0.15 A, and the constant-power Pico load model of build/15 (0.145 A at VSYS 4.5 V) rises to 0.146-0.151 A at LAB5 5.02 V and 0.154-0.159 A at LAB5 4.80 V, 0.161 A with the 0.287 ohm E3_PICO_VSYS copper (MODEL; review RV-CTRL6-E2-2: the PTC resistance below trip rises with temperature and Bourns publishes R only at 23 C, so the load reaches IOSmin at about 1.52 ohm of F302 at LAB5 4.80 V); hence R397 140k (IOSmin 0.165 A) instead of 150k (IOSmin 0.154 A), review RV-CTRL6-E-1.; Lifecycle: MF-MSMF050 is marked 'currently available but not recommended for new designs' in Bourns MF-MSMF REV. BE 09/26 (page 1 legend, read 2026-11-22). Kept because it is stocked (JLCPCB C17313, 99054 on 2026-11-22) while the non-NRND MF-MSMF050/16X-2 (C49303322) had stock 0 on 2026-11-22 and its R1max 1.3 ohm would lower the VSYS margin further (0.161 A load at LAB5 4.80 V against IOSmin 0.165 A, MODEL); review RV-CTRL6-E-2, build/15 row 'PTC: стан життєвого циклу (W2 CTRL-6)'.; Reflow soldering only, as F301 (Bourns MF-MSMF REV. BE solder reflow recommendations, read 2026-11-22)." (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
