(property "Reference" "R398" (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) ))
(property "Value" "1k" (at 0 -2.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) ))
(property "Footprint" "Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric" (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
(property "Datasheet" "project design (W2 CTRL-6, build/15)" (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
(property "Description" " | design | W2 CTRL-6 (review RV-CTRL5-S2-4; orchestrator decision: option (a), a series resistor in the gate drive): R398 sits between the gate node E3_FAN_PG (Q304.1, R367.1) and the Q303 drain (E3_FAN_PD), so a Q304 gate-oxide breakdown or a solder bridge across R367 (LAB5 to E3_FAN_PG) drives at most 5.25 V / 1 kohm = 5.3 mA through the gate copper and Q303 (27.6 mW in this 0.1 W part, MODEL), instead of PTC or F102 current; placed at Q304.1 it would not cover the R367 bridge. Q304 on: gate at LAB5 x 1k / 101k = 0.05 V, VGS -4.95 V (RDS(on) < 60 mOhm is specified at -4.5 V, AO3401A Rev 3.1); turn-on through 1 kohm with Qg 7 nC at -4.5 V about 1.4 us, Ciss 645 pF: tau 0.65 us (MODEL); turn-off through R367 100k unchanged. The fan is switched DC on/off from GP18, no PWM (firmware/pico/README.md)." (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
